kubectl get namespaces

. Create Namespace
kubectl create namespace devops

Creates a new namespace called devops.

2. List Namespaces
kubectl get namespaces

Shows all namespaces in the Kubernetes cluster.

3. Short Command
kubectl get ns

ns is the short form of namespaces.

4. Get Specific Namespace
kubectl get namespace devops

Displays information about the devops namespace.

5. Describe Namespace
kubectl describe namespace devops

Shows detailed information about the namespace.

6. Create Namespace Using YAML
kubectl apply -f namespace.yaml

Creates the namespace using a YAML specification file.

7. Delete Namespace
kubectl delete namespace devops

Deletes the devops namespace and its resources.

8. Check Pods in Namespace
kubectl get pods -n devops

Shows Pods running inside the devops namespace.

9. Check All Resources
kubectl get all -n devops

Shows Pods, Services, Deployments, ReplicaSets, and other supported resources in the namespace.

10. Get Pods from All Namespaces
kubectl get pods -A

Shows Pods from every namespace.

11. Set Default Namespace
kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=devops

Sets devops as the default namespace for the current Kubernetes context.

12. Check Current Namespace
kubectl config view --minify --output 'jsonpath={..namespace}'

Displays the namespace configured for the current context.

13. Create Namespace with Labels
kubectl create namespace devops --dry-run=client -o yaml

Generates the Namespace YAML without creating it.

14. Export Namespace YAML
kubectl get namespace devops -o yaml

Displays the Namespace configuration in YAML format.

15. Get Resources in Namespace
kubectl get pods,svc,deploy -n devops

Shows Pods, Services, and Deployments in the devops namespace.

